-- title:
--   Sign-based fast decoding equals exact decoding
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group, $H=G[2]$, $R_S$ the ordered pair-sum count of a finite support, and $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{s\in S}\chi(s)$. Assume $G$ finite. Let $U$ contain the nonzero support of observed square $R$, let $h$ be a sound and complete partial halving solver, and let $o=(R,v)$ for an arbitrary bank $\chi_i$, $i\in I$. Select indices $\iota(0),\ldots,\iota(r-1)$ and coordinates $e:H\cong(\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z)^r$ so that $\chi_{\iota(j)}(u)=(-1)^{e(u)_j}$. Assume each selected reading is nonzero on every triple. Use those selected readings and $v$ for sign recovery. Then
--
--   $$\operatorname{FastSignDecoder}(U,h,\chi,o,\iota,e)=\{S:|S|=3,\operatorname{Obs}_\chi(S)=o\}.$$
--
--   The final exact observation filter remains part of the decoder.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/RecohFastDecoder.lean, lines 305–321; source file SHA-256 d84bc4908e0c9ab4ae54de4f0901e08828a787fa98a3987c63969ea57c85e8da; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.recoh_sign_fast_decoder_eq_exact

